CRC32(3)                       P32W Unix                        CRC32(3)

NAME
       crc32 - the CRC-32 checksum of zip and gzip

SYNOPSIS
       #include <deflate.h>

       unsigned crc32(unsigned crc, const void *buf, unsigned n);

DESCRIPTION
       crc32 returns the CRC-32 of the n bytes at buf, the checksum
       that zip, gzip and PNG files carry (the polynomial 0xEDB88320,
       reflected, with the register inverted before and after). Call
       it with crc 0 for the first piece of data, and with the result
       so far for each later piece: the result is the CRC of all the
       pieces in turn.

       It works a byte at a time through a table of 256 words, built
       on the first call.

RETURN VALUE
       The CRC.

EXAMPLES
       unsigned crc = 0;
       while ((n = read(fd, buf, sizeof buf)) > 0)
           crc = crc32(crc, buf, n);
       printf("%08x\n", crc);

       crc32(0, "123456789", 9) is 0xcbf43926.

SEE ALSO
       gzip(1), zip(1), cmp(1), deflate(3)
